{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## REMEDY APPLIED — 1288 re-pushed, now 6 files\n\nBoth edits from the previous comment are in, and the sweep found a THIRD thing the first pass missed:\n\n 1. `_snapshot_schema.py` — the TypedDict `parent: JiraParent` was widened to `JiraParent | None` with the\n    three-state contract documented, **and the runtime JSON SCHEMA at :157 was the actual cause of\n    `test_fetch_snapshot_conforms_to_schema` (\"None is not of type 'object'\")** — the TypedDict edit alone\n    would not have fixed it. Now `\"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"]`, which is **exactly the shape `assignee`\n    two lines above already uses**, so this follows the schema's own precedent rather than inventing one.\n    `required: [key]` still applies when the value IS an object, per JSON Schema semantics.\n 2. `tests/integration/.../test_jira_fixtures.py:86` — inverted preserving intent, with the reasoning in\n    the assertion comments. Was `\"parent\" not in epic`; now asserts the key is PRESENT **and** falsy.\n    Strictly stronger: the old form could not distinguish a queried-parentless issue from a failed or\n    truncated read.\n\nCONSUMER SWEEP, now actually done (the AC I skipped before the first push). Grepped both `src/` and\n`tests/` for the two forms that change behaviour — `\"parent\" in` / `\"parent\" not in` and\n`fields[\"parent\"]` indexing. Only real hits outside this ticket's own files:\n  * `dispatch_one.py:546  _has_parent_op = \"parent\" in fields` — OUTBOUND mutation payload, not the\n    snapshot. Unaffected.\n  * `test_inbound_differ_field_contract.py:131`, `test_parent_detach_sync.py:106,153` — all inspect\n    `entry[\"fields\"]` / `m.fields` (mutation payloads), not snapshot entries. Unaffected, and they pass.\nEvery snapshot consumer reads `.get(\"parent\")` and branches on falsiness, so an explicit `None` is\nindistinguishable from absent to all of them.\n\nVerification: `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/` + `diffing/` + `fetch/` → **369 passed**;\n`jira_contract/` + `diffing/` after the final rebase → **306 passed**. `make lint` and `make typecheck`\n(419 files) clean. Rebased onto current `gerrit/main` before pushing and confirmed the commit is exactly\nthe intended **6 files / 690 insertions** — `git diff --stat gerrit/main` showed 15 files only because main\nhad advanced, which is the diff direction, not contamination. Change-Id preserved across the amend\n(verified explicitly, since `--amend -F -` regenerates it).\n\nFile impact widened to six paths to match."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785769929391667001,"uuid":"0571a937-edeb-4b99-99da-526dd56713dc"}